   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "הָיְתָה כְּתוּבָה בְּסַם כּוּ׳. סַם — סַמָּא. סִקְרָא, אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה: סְקַרְתָּא שְׁמַהּ. קוֹמוֹס — קוֹמָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If one reads from a Megilla that «was written with sam» or with sikra or with komos or with kankantom, he has not fulfilled his obligation. The Gemara identifies these writing materials: «Sam» is what is called in Aramaic «samma.» With regard to «sikra, Rabba bar bar Ḥana said: Its name» in Aramaic is «sikreta,» a type of red paint. «Komos» is what is called «koma,» a tree resin."
  }
 ],
